<threat_model>
## Trust Boundaries

| Boundary | Description |
|----------|-------------|
| User role → nav visibility | OWNER check gates tab visibility |
| URL parameter → section rendering | Non-OWNER ai-key URL redirected to general |
| Client → clipboard API | Full key available only in toast action closure |
| Toast lifecycle → key reference | setToast(null) releases plaintext closure after timeout |

## STRIDE Threat Register

| Threat ID | Category | Component | Disposition | Mitigation Plan |
|-----------|----------|-----------|-------------|-----------------|
| T-03-01 | Elevation of Privilege | SettingsShell.tsx | mitigate | `visibleNavItems` filters 'ai-key' to `role === 'OWNER'` only; `initialSection` redirects non-OWNER URL access to 'general' |
| T-03-02 | Information Disclosure | GeminiKeySection.tsx | mitigate | Full key only in `navigator.clipboard.writeText` closure within toast action; toast auto-clears after 8s via `setToast(null)` releasing closure reference |
| T-03-03 | Information Disclosure | Toast memory | mitigate | `setToast(null)` on timeout and on action click releases the `savedKey` closure, preventing long-lived plaintext in memory (Pitfall 6 from RESEARCH.md) |
| T-03-04 | Spoofing | SettingsShell RBAC | mitigate | Client-side RBAC is defense-in-depth only; actual enforcement is in API handlers (Plan 02 T-02-01). Non-OWNER fetching GeminiKeySection data gets 403 from API. |
| T-03-05 | Tampering | Input validation | mitigate | Enter key prevented on input (no accidental submission); save button disabled when input empty |
</threat_model>

